  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains two complete program listings (Bachelor of Arts in Project Management and Bachelor of Arts in Psychology) plus truncated Associate of Arts in Business and Bachelor of Arts in Social and Criminal Justice listings; the request did not specify which program, so Project Management (first complete listing) was drafted. Confirm the intended program.",
    "ECO 204 (major) also satisfies 3 credits of Global Campus Foundations requirements, but the capture does not say which specific Global Campus Foundations course it replaces; listed items sum to 123 credits against the 120 total because of this 3-credit overlap.",
    "GEN 101 Developing Skills and Strategies for Success (3 credits) is scheduled as the first course and satisfies 3 elective credits; it is not listed separately to avoid double-counting within the 45-credit elective block.",
    "Bachelor students transferring fewer than 30 credits must also take GEN 104 (3 credits, counts toward electives); the capture does not give GEN 104's title.",
    "The capture states Global Campus Foundations courses may be substituted but does not specify allowable substitutions.",
    "Residency: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University as a matriculated student; the capture does not tie this to specific courses, so no individual requirement is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "A minimum of 30 upper-division credits (including 18 upper-division credits in the major) is required; the capture does not identify which electives must be upper-division.",
    "BUS 402 must be taken last in the program; the capture does not label it a capstone.",
    "Quantitative Reasoning requirement must be met before BUS 401 and BUS 308; the capture does not state which course satisfies Quantitative Reasoning beyond MAT 222 appearing in the Foundations sequence."
  ],
